<svg class="wm-svg" viewBox="50 0 880 572" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="wm-title wm-desc"><title id="wm-title">A world model inside the brain</title><desc id="wm-desc">Inside an outline of a brain, where clusters of voxels light up and fade in dodger blue, light coral and medium sea green, as in an fMRI scan: the words world model at the top; beneath them three parts — a person looking in a mirror for causal knowledge about the self, the Earth for causal knowledge about the world, and activities with the points they are worth, good or bad, for intrinsic goals — which feed down into three task representations drawn as small state-transition diagrams. Beside each arrow into a task, a Shepard-style generalization gradient — inheritance decaying with dissimilarity — marks how much of the priors that task inherits, from most on the left to least on the right. Each part can be clicked for an explanation.</desc><style>.wm-h{font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:30px;font-weight:700;fill:#000000;letter-spacing:.14em}.wm-lab{font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:19px;font-weight:700;fill:#121f3a}.wm-cap{font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.5px;fill:#2b2b2b;letter-spacing:.06em}.wm-sym{font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:700}.wm-emo{font-family:"Apple Color Emoji","Segoe UI Emoji","Noto Color Emoji",sans-serif}.wm-pts{font-family:Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:19px;font-weight:700;fill:#000000}.wm-node{cursor:pointer;outline:none}.wm-node .wm-disc{transition:stroke-width .15s}.wm-node:hover .wm-disc,.wm-node:focus-visible .wm-disc,.wm-node.is-open .wm-disc{stroke-width:5}.wm-node:focus-visible .wm-h,.wm-node.is-open .wm-h,.wm-node:hover .wm-h{opacity:.75}</style><defs><linearGradient id="wm-glass" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#f2f9fd"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#b8d8ee"/></linearGradient><clipPath id="wm-mirror